# rule.require.git-release-confidence

## .what
when a human says "release into prod", act: stage all changes, drive the normal workflow, no re-ask
1. `rhx git.release --watch` — verify every gate passed
2. `rhx git.release --into prod --mode apply --watch` — full feat → main → prod cycle

## .the only judgment
did cicd pass? green → ship. red → fix the cause or retry a proven flake (`rhx show.gh.test.errors`), then re-check. never leave main dirty

## .why
the gates absorb the risk: full suite + acceptance before merge, so a broken build cannot reach prod. a second confirm adds friction, not safety

## .routine bumps ride along
rhachet/role package bumps, `.agent/keyrack.yml`, `.claude/settings.json`, generated manifests — in scope by default
stop and flag only: a secret VALUE in a tracked file; a dependency downgrade or suspicious pin

## .trigger
explicit human "release into prod". without it, never release on your own

## .enforcement
- re-ask after "release into prod" = nitpick
- extra checks beyond "did cicd pass?" = nitpick
- ask whether routine bumps belong = nitpick
- stop at main when asked for prod = blocker
